AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0000017> "Note that this term is classified as a type of abnormal cell shape, because wild-type cells are never seen with the proportions (length:diameter ratio) observed in elongated cells. Small cells, in contrast, have the same proportions as a subset of wild-type cells, and simply do not grow to the full length seen in wild type.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0000017> "elongated cell")
