# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001047> (obsolete mitotic catastrophe)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001047> "OBSOLETE. A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which a cell proceeds through the mitotic metaphase/anaphase transition in the presence of an uncorrected problem (such as chromosome structure or kinetochore attachment), and as a result undergoes abnormal nuclear division and subsequently dies.")
