AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001387> "For S. pombe, high temperature usually means above 32 degrees C. Use this term to annotate experiments in which a culture is grown at high temperature, and then the number of cells viable enough to form a colony upon return to standard or low temperature is measured and compared to wild type.")
