# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> (increased minichromosome loss)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "A cell phenotype in which minichromosomes are lost at a higher frequency than normal. Minichromosome loss occurs when one or both daughter cells do not inherit copies of a minichromosome from the mother cell, and may result from failure of minichromosome replication or segregation.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "midori")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "2012-12-18T14:36:26Z")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "fission_yeast_phenotype")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "minichromosome maintenance defect")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "FYPO:0001859")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "Note that in budding yeast, increased plasmid loss is often called a minichromosome maintenance defect, because \"minichromosome\" is roughly synonymous with an autonomously replicated and segregated plasmid in that organism. In fission yeast, a minichromosome is a large portion of a chromosome, usually about half of chromosome 3, that replicates and segregates autonomously. For smaller autonomously replicating and segregating constructs, consider 'increased plasmid loss' (FYPO:0000786).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> "increased minichromosome loss")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0000002>)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001859> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0003037>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0001860> (increased minichromosome loss during meiotic cell cycle)

