AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0002723> "Note that normal cells do not accumulate detectable levels of any pigment; for this reason, FYPO does not include separate terms for 'increased' and 'abnormal' pigment accumulation. Also note that pigment accumulates in the vacuole. This term refers to GO:0033059 'cellular pigmentation', rather than GO:0043482 'cellular pigment accumulation', because GO:0043482 has paths to 'response to stimulus' in GO.")
