# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0003489> (abnormal mitotic cell cycle regulation during cellular response to ionizing radiation)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0003489> "A cellular response phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the regulation of the mitotic cell cycle in response to ionizing radiation is abnormal. Normally, cell cycle progression is slowed or arrested transiently following exposure to ionizing radiation. The most common abnormality is for the cell cycle to progress as in the absence of ionizing radiation.")
