# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> (normal zygotic meiosis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:22558440") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25891897") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "A cellular process phenotype in which the meiotic nuclear divisions are normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during a cycle of zygotic meiosis and sporulation. Zygotic meiosis and sporulation take place under conditions of continuous nitrogen starvation, in which haploid cells of the opposite mating types conjugate to form diploid zygotes that proceed immediately to undergo meiosis and sporulation.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "midori")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "2015-08-07T11:44:07Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:vw") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "normal meiosis during zygotic meiosis")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "GO:0140013") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "normal zygotic meiotic nuclear division")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "fission_yeast_phenotype")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "FYPO:0004795")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> "normal zygotic meiosis")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004795> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0000478>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> (normal azygotic meiosis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:22558440") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25891897") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "A cellular process phenotype in which the meiotic nuclear divisions are normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during a cycle of azygotic meiosis and sporulation. Azygotic meiosis and sporulation occur when meiosis takes place within a diploid cell rather than in a zygote produced by sporulation. Zygotes can resume vegetative growth and form colonies of diploid cells if returned to rich media before commitment to meiosis; under nitrogen starvation, diploid cells heterozygous for mating type will undergo azygotic meiosis. Azygotic asci have a characteristic linear morphology resembling that of a single vegetatively growing cell.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "midori")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "2015-08-07T11:55:56Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "GO:0140013") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "normal azygotic meiotic nuclear division")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:vw") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "normal meiosis during azygotic meiosis")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "fission_yeast_phenotype")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "FYPO:0004796")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> "normal azygotic meiosis")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004796> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0000478>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> (normal azygotic meiosis I)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:22558440") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25891897") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "A cellular process phenotype in which the first meiotic nuclear division is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type) during a cycle of azygotic meiosis and sporulation. Azygotic meiosis and sporulation occur when meiosis takes place within a diploid cell rather than in a zygote produced by sporulation. Zygotes can resume vegetative growth and form colonies of diploid cells if returned to rich media before commitment to meiosis; under nitrogen starvation, diploid cells heterozygous for mating type will undergo azygotic meiosis. Azygotic asci have a characteristic linear morphology resembling that of a single vegetatively growing cell.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:created_by <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "midori")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "2015-08-07T11:57:35Z")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "GO:0140013") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "normal azygotic first meiotic nuclear division")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:vw") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "normal meiosis I during azygotic meiosis")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "fission_yeast_phenotype")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:id <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "FYPO:0004797")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> "normal azygotic meiosis I")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004797> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0003563>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004798> (abolished azygotic meiosis II)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:22558440") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:25891897") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004798> "A cellular process phenotype in which the second meiotic nuclear division does not occur during a cycle of azygotic meiosis and sporulation. Azygotic meiosis and sporulation occur when meiosis takes place within a diploid cell rather than in a zygote produced by sporulation. Zygotes can resume vegetative growth and form colonies of diploid cells if returned to rich media before commitment to meiosis; under nitrogen starvation, diploid cells heterozygous for mating type will undergo azygotic meiosis. Azygotic asci have a characteristic linear morphology resembling that of a single vegetatively growing cell.")
