AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0004841> "Note that this term can be used to annotate any case where a protein is found in the nucleus in a mutant, but not in wild type. In some cases, there may be enough additional information to annotate to 'abnormal protein localization' (FYPO:0000443) or one of its descendants. We recommend noting which protein(s) were used in the assay when annotating to this term. Note that FYPO uses \"glucose starvation\" to refer specifically to conditions in which glucose is scarce enough to trigger mating, meiosis, and sporulation. For phenotypes observed in the presence of enough glucose to prevent cells from mating, use a term that specifies \"during vegetative growth\" plus a condition to indicate low glucose.")
