# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0005373> (normal mitotic cell cycle regulation during cellular response to methyl methanesulfonate)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0005373> "A cellular response phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the regulation of the mitotic cell cycle in response to methyl methanesulfonate (MMS) is normal (i.e. indistinguishable from wild type). Normally, cell cycle progression is slowed or arrested transiently following exposure to MMS.")
