# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0005427> (elongated J-shaped vegetative cell with curved interphase microtubules)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:11739790") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:vw") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0005427> "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetatively growing cell is elongated, is curved along the long axis to form a \"J\" shape, and contains cytoplasmic microtubules that curve to follow the long axis of the cell. In a curved cell, the long axis follows a smooth bend rather than a straight line. In a J-shaped cell, the curve is centered away from the midpoint of the long axis of the cell.")
