# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0006248> (increased centromere clustering at nuclear periphery during mitosis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:28825727") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0006248> "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of centromeres and associated kinetochores into a cluster at the nuclear periphery is increased during mitosis. Normally, centromere-kinetochore complexes cluster near the old spindle pole body during interphase of the mitotic cell cycle, but are not as tightly clustered during mitosis.")
