AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:30475921") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0006790> "A biological process phenotype in which meiotic drive occurs to a lower extent than normal, or does not occur at all, despite the presence of a gene or allele that normally causes drive. Meiotic drive results in the unequal transmission of alleles, haplotypes, or chromosomes from a parental genome to such that are unequally represented (i.e. the \"driver\" is overrepresented) among the surviving products of meiosis.")
