# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0006822> (viable small vegetative cell with normal cell growth rate)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0006822> "A cell morphology phenotype in which a vegetatively growing cell is viable and elongates at a normal rate, but divides when a shorter time than normal has elapsed since the previous cell division. Daughter cells therefore have an abnormally low volume. Note that these small viable cells result from a cell cycle size regulation defect.")
