# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0007784> (decreased protein localization to protein aggregate center)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:32075773") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:33946513") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mah") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0007784> "A cell phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle in which the localization of a protein to protein aggregate centers is decreased. Protein aggregate centers are composed of chaperones and misfolded proteins, and are reversibly formed in the nucleus and cytosol to shield thermosensitive proteins from degradation until conditions allow disaggregation and refolding.")
