# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0007968> (cut with mitotic spindle microtubules protruding beyond spindle pole body)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PMID:26031557") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:mlr") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "PomBase:vw") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FYPO_0007968> "An inviable phenotype observed in the vegetative growth phase of the life cycle after normal chromosome separation in which pushing forces exerted by microtubules protruding from the spindle pole bodies displace one of the daughter nuclei to the site of cytokinesis. The septum then physically divides that nucleus into two parts, giving rise to inviable daughter cell.")
